 6. Quick hits 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 The Savannah River Site, as seen from space in 2021. Photo: HUM Images/Universal Images Group via Getty Images

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 🏥 One person was injured in a fire at the Savannah River National Laboratory, part of the Savannah River Site in South Carolina. Workers were initially ordered to shelter in place. Radiological surveys found no contamination. 

 Why it matters: This is a rare incident at one of America's most consequential nuke-producing installations. (Expect few follow-up details.) 💭 My thought bubble: People need to chill on X . So, so, so much misinformation and fearmongering. 🛒 Salesforce is buying Rune Technologies — but did not say for how much.

 Why it matters: It's being billed as Salesforce's "most significant national security-focused acquisition." Rune is already working with the U.S. Army and Marine Corps. 💭 My thought bubble: My colleague Chris Metinko with Pro Deals has the full story, here . 🏭 BWX Technologies and Antares struck a multiyear agreement for production of tri-structural isotropic nuclear fuel. It will be made at the former's Lynchburg, Virginia, facility.

 Why it matters: "We achieved criticality with BWXT fuel, and it's what will power our electricity-producing reactor, Mark-1, in 2027," Antares CEO Jordan Bramble said in a statement. 💭 My thought bubble: I visited BWXT and took a peek at Project Pele in September. More, here . 💵 Re:Build said it secured $2.1 billion in new funding. The investment was led by General Catalyst and JPMorgan Chase's Strategic Investment Group.

 Why it matters: "The products and companies emerging from our ecosystem prove we can help restore America's industrial might," co-founder Jeff Wilke said in a statement. 💭 My thought bubble: Co-founder Miles Arnone will join us onstage Nov. 19 at the Future of Defense Summit in Washington! 
 
